  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35734000",
      "title": "The json() Utility Function",
      "sourceHash": "c61b5d347143465f7f9c5adc1c08c13309450777d0dd3074769933729f823d63",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 3.93,
          "en": "Now when using React router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.93,
          "end": 6.51,
          "en": "you will from time to time construct responses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.51,
          "end": 7.65,
          "en": "as we're doing it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.65,
          "end": 10.98,
          "en": "especially when it comes to throwing errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.98,
          "end": 14.043,
          "en": "For all the reasons mentioned in the previous lectures.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.21,
          "end": 18.72,
          "en": "Now, constructing responses manually like this is possible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.72,
          "end": 20.16,
          "en": "but a bit annoying.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.16,
          "end": 24.423,
          "en": "That's why React router gives you a little helper, utility.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.44,
          "end": 27.99,
          "en": "Instead of creating your response like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.99,
          "end": 29.73,
          "en": "and returning it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.73,
          "end": 33,
          "en": "you can return the result of calling json,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33,
          "end": 34.47,
          "en": "written like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.47,
          "end": 37.89,
          "en": "And json is a function that can be imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.89,
          "end": 39.573,
          "en": "from react-router-dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.1,
          "end": 44.91,
          "en": "Now json is a function that creates a response object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.91,
          "end": 47.643,
          "en": "that includes data in the json format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.72,
          "end": 52.08,
          "en": "To this json function, you simply pass your data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.08,
          "end": 53.97,
          "en": "that should be included in the response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.97,
          "end": 55.92,
          "en": "in my case, my object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.92,
          "end": 59.13,
          "en": "and you don't need to convert it to json manually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.13,
          "end": 61.113,
          "en": "Instead, that will be done for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.22,
          "end": 65.28,
          "en": "And you can pass a second argument where you can set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.28,
          "end": 69.3,
          "en": "that extra response metadata like this status.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.3,
          "end": 72.303,
          "en": "And here I set this status to 500 again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.2,
          "end": 74.85,
          "en": "Now with this json function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.85,
          "end": 77.7,
          "en": "you don't just have to type less code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.7,
          "end": 80.61,
          "en": "but in the place where you use that response data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.61,
          "end": 85.17,
          "en": "you also don't have to parse the json format manually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.17,
          "end": 87.81,
          "en": "Instead, you can simplify the code to this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.81,
          "end": 90.03,
          "en": "because the parsing will now be done",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.03,
          "end": 92.163,
          "en": "by React router for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.72,
          "end": 96.3,
          "en": "And therefore, now here if we break this again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.3,
          "end": 100.97999999999999,
          "en": "by sending the request to an invalid URL in this loader",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.97999999999999,
          "end": 103.59,
          "en": "you see we got the same error message as before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.59,
          "end": 107.13,
          "en": "but now with less code to be written from our side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.13,
          "end": 109.74000000000001,
          "en": "And that of course is a great simplification",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.74000000000001,
          "end": 112.83,
          "en": "and hence it is quite common to use this json function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.83,
          "end": 116.013,
          "en": "for building responses with less effort.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.85,
          "end": 118.50399999999999,
          "en": "With that, I'll again fix this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.50399999999999,
          "end": 122.31,
          "en": "URL here so that we do fetch events successfully again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.31,
          "end": 125.013,
          "en": "but you should keep this json function in mind.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
